"r": "Key D is correct. Section 5 vests federal executive power in the President, and external affairs is an exclusive federal matter. The President formulates and directs foreign policy through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. One minor imprecision in the explanation: the National Assembly's role is not limited to treaties. Under Section 12 it domesticates treaties by enacting them into law; it does not strictly ratify them. The Senate also confirms ambassadors, and the National Assembly must sanction any declaration of war. The item itself is sound and at UTME level."
